    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2023-08-23T04:49:12Z",
    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Looks interesting, thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nOn one hand, looking at implementation it might indeed be a good fit for 'mini.misc'. On the other, I personally need more convincing to override such basic mappings as `p` and `P` and making them exported functions is not that user friendly.\r\n\r\nAlso, you can achieve a very similar functionality by tweaking `o`/`O` instead and use `grr` from [mini.operators](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-operators.md):\r\n\r\n```vim\r\nnnoremap <Leader>o o<Space><BS><Esc>\r\nnnoremap <Leader>O O<Space><BS><Esc>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThese variants will create new line below/above current line with \"correct\" indentation and ending up in Normal mode. After that, doing `grr` will replace this line with proper register and `[count]`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Looks interesting, thanks for suggestion!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">On one hand, looking at implementation it might indeed be a good fit for 'mini.misc'. On the other, I personally need more convincing to override such basic mappings as <code class=\"notranslate\">p</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">P</code> and making them exported functions is not that user friendly.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, you can achieve a very similar functionality by tweaking <code class=\"notranslate\">o</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">O</code> instead and use <code class=\"notranslate\">grr</code> from <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-operators.md\">mini.operators</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-viml notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"nnoremap &lt;Leader&gt;o o&lt;Space&gt;&lt;BS&gt;&lt;Esc&gt;\nnnoremap &lt;Leader&gt;O O&lt;Space&gt;&lt;BS&gt;&lt;Esc&gt;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">nnoremap</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;Leader&gt;</span><span class=\"pl-s\">o o<span class=\"pl-e\">&lt;Space&gt;&lt;BS&gt;&lt;Esc&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-s\"></span><span class=\"pl-k\">nnoremap</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;Leader&gt;</span><span class=\"pl-s\">O O<span class=\"pl-e\">&lt;Space&gt;&lt;BS&gt;&lt;Esc&gt;</span></span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These variants will create new line below/above current line with \"correct\" indentation and ending up in Normal mode. After that, doing <code class=\"notranslate\">grr</code> will replace this line with proper register and <code class=\"notranslate\">[count]</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Looks interesting, thanks for suggestion!\nOn one hand, looking at implementation it might indeed be a good fit for 'mini.misc'. On the other, I personally need more convincing to override such basic mappings as p and P and making them exported functions is not that user friendly.\nAlso, you can achieve a very similar functionality by tweaking o/O instead and use grr from mini.operators:\nnnoremap <Leader>o o<Space><BS><Esc>\nnnoremap <Leader>O O<Space><BS><Esc>\nThese variants will create new line below/above current line with \"correct\" indentation and ending up in Normal mode. After that, doing grr will replace this line with proper register and [count].",
