            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "Hmmm, I think this would work for my usecase but I can't seem to get it to work:\r\n```\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<leader>o', 'o<Space><BS><Esc>grr', {\r\n    desc = 'Paste after with proper indentation',\r\n    noremap = true,\r\n    silent = true\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis creates a new line with proper indentation but then just types \"r\".  If I do the keystrokes myself it works - pasting in the content with the proper indentation.  Any ideas?",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hmmm, I think this would work for my usecase but I can't seem to get it to work:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;leader&gt;o', 'o&lt;Space&gt;&lt;BS&gt;&lt;Esc&gt;grr', {\n    desc = 'Paste after with proper indentation',\n    noremap = true,\n    silent = true\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;leader&gt;o', 'o&lt;Space&gt;&lt;BS&gt;&lt;Esc&gt;grr', {\n    desc = 'Paste after with proper indentation',\n    noremap = true,\n    silent = true\n})\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This creates a new line with proper indentation but then just types \"r\".  If I do the keystrokes myself it works - pasting in the content with the proper indentation.  Any ideas?</p>",
            "bodyText": "Hmmm, I think this would work for my usecase but I can't seem to get it to work:\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<leader>o', 'o<Space><BS><Esc>grr', {\n    desc = 'Paste after with proper indentation',\n    noremap = true,\n    silent = true\n})\n\nThis creates a new line with proper indentation but then just types \"r\".  If I do the keystrokes myself it works - pasting in the content with the proper indentation.  Any ideas?",
